    "k": "m1",
    "title": "Walk the brick blocks after dark",
    "theme": "outdoors",
    "paragraph": "String lights go on over four brick blocks around dusk, and the street turns into a different place. Start at the top by the church steps, drift down past the buskers and the patios, duck into the gear basement for ten minutes, and finish at the scoop shop on the corner. It is a slow walk on purpose. Nobody is in a hurry here after dark, and you should not be either. Come back on a Saturday morning to see it the other way.",
