    "title": "Swim off the north beach before work",
    "theme": "water",
    "paragraph": "The water is calmest before eight, when the beach is just you and the dog walkers. Park by the pines, leave your shoes on the steps, and swim out to the second buoy and back. The city tests the water twice a week, so check the board by the lifeguard stand first. Then towel off, get a coffee at the stand on the bike path, and show up to work with wet hair and a better attitude than anyone in the room.",
